          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Overconvergent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+analytic+geometry"} global analytic geometry
            is a setting for global analytic geometry that allows the definition of strict and non-strict analytic spaces over an arbitrary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+rings"} Banach rings
            = succeed "Banach" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Banach+ring"} pseudo-Banach ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+motivic+homotopy+theory"} analytic motivic homotopy theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+global+analytic+geometry"} derived global analytic geometry
          %h2#BasicIdeas Basic ideas
          %p
            The basic building blocks for overconvergent global analytic geometry over a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+ring"} Banach ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,{\vert\cdot\vert})
            are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydiscs"} polydiscs
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (in the strict situation) or arbitrary real radius (in the non-strict situation), and more generally, by strict (or non-strict) rational domains in them. This gives two categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi RatAlg
                    %mi R
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RatAlg_R^s
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi RatAlg
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RatAlg_R
            of rational domain algebras that actually form
            %a{:href => "geometry+%28for+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes%29#Pregeometry"} pre-geometries
            in the sense of Lurie.
          %p
            One then defines analytic (resp. derived analytic) algebras as functors (resp. homotopical functors) of functions on the categories of rational domain algebras. The various types of finitely presented analytic algebras define various types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometries
            in Lurie’s sense. One may then define analytic (resp. derived analytic) stacks as functors (resp. homotopical functors) of points on analytic (resp. derived analytic) algebras.
          %p
            This gives in particular four categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi An
                      %mi R
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} An_R^\dagger
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi An
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo †
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} An_R^{\dagger,s}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi DAn
                    %mi R
                    %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DAn_R^\dagger
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi DAn
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo †
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DAn_R^{\dagger,s}
            of strict and non-strict overconvergent derived and non-derived analytic spaces.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ProjectiveLine Projective line
          %p
            One may define the strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+line"} projective line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1_R
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            by pasting the overconvergent unit disc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo †
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^1=\mathbb{M}(R\{T\}^\dagger)
            with itself along its boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo †
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ST
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)=\mathbb{M}(R\{T,S\}^\dagger/(ST-1))
            by the map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mapsto 1/T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            equipped with its usual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+absolute+value"} archimedean absolute value
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arakelov+geometry"} Arakelov geometry
          %h3#UnitaryGroup Unitary group
          %p
            One may try to use a similar construction to define higher dimensional global analogs of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+groups"} unitary groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydisc"} polydisc
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi ij
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mi max
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi ij
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M_n^{\leq 1}
                  \:= \{(a_{ij})\in M_n,\;\max_{i,j}|a_{ij}|\leq 1\}
          %p
            in the (non-strict analytic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n=\mathbb{A}^{n^2}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            does not restrict to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n^{\leq 1}\times_R M_n^{\leq 1}\to M_n^{\leq 1},
          %p
            this matrix polydisc is not a monoid. This implies that the naive definition of a global analytic version of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(n)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\{(A,B)\in M_n^{\leq 1},\;A B = B A = I\},
          %p only gives a strict analytic space that is not equipped with an analytic group structure (except if one works in a non-archimedean setting).
          %p
            One may however associate to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n^{\leq 1}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+space"} analytic space
            (a kind of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi BM
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  BM_n^{\leq 1}_{[k]}\coloneqq
                  \\{(A_i)\in (M_n^{\leq 1})^{k},\;
                  \\prod_{j\in [s]} A_j\in (M_n^{\leq 1})^{s}\;\forall f:[s]\hookrightarrow [k]\}.
          %p
            One may then define the
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BU(n)
            to be given by the analytic sub-groupoid of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\GL_n
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∩
                  %msubsup
                    %mi BM
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  BU(n)
                  \\coloneqq
                  B\GL_n\cap BM_n^{\leq 1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Remark now that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi BM
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BM_n^{\leq 1}
            is a strict simplicial analytic space, because it is a subspace of the strict simplicial space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [k]\mapsto (M_n^{\leq 1})^k
            defined by strict inequalities. One may also see
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BU(n)
            as a closed strict simplicial analytic subspace of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi BM
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi BM
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BM_n^{\leq 1}\times BM_n^{\leq 1}
            of pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AB
                    %mo =
                    %mi BA
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AB=BA=I
          %p We may now look at what we get over various standard Banach rings:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z},|\cdot|_0)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
                is isomorphic to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi GL
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_{n,\mathbb{Z}}
            %li
              %p
                Over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ℚ
                          %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Q}_p,|\cdot|_p)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
                is such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ℚ
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)(\mathbb{Q}_p)=\GL_n(\mathbb{Z}_p)
            %li
              %p
                Over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z},|\cdot|_\infty)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
                is not an analytic group, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)(\mathbb{Z},|\cdot|_\infty)
                is closer to what people usually denote
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mo ±
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \GL_n(\mathbb{F}_{\{\pm 1\}})
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_{\{\pm 1\}}
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
                in Durov’s sense.
            %li
              %p
                Over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
                contains the classical unitary group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)(\mathbb{C})
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=(a_{ij})
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi max
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi max
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi ij
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|A\|_{max}:=\max(|a_{ij}|)\leq \|A\|_2,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|A\|_2
                is the operator norm for the hermitian norm on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi BU
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi BU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BU_{n}(\mathbb{C})\to BU(n)(\mathbb{C})
              %p
                from the simplicial classifying space of the classical unitary group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{n}(\C)
                to the complex points of the simplicial “classifying space”
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi BU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BU(n)
          %p
            It is also clearly compact (contained in a product of polydiscs) and contained in the non-strict analytic group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \GL_{n}(\mathbb{C})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)(\mathbb{C})
            is a maximal compact subgroup, we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            is indeed the complex unitary group over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          %h3#arithmetic_principal_unitary_bundles Arithmetic principal unitary bundles
          %p
            The good properties of the global analytic unitary group
            %strong may
            imply that there is a natural bijection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi K
                  %mo \
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0(BU(n)(\mathbb{Z},|\cdot|_\infty))\cong
                  K\backslash \GL_n(\mathbb{A})/\GL_n(\mathbb{Q}),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the maximal compact subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n,\mathbb{R})\times \GL_n(\hat{\mathbb{Z}})
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GL
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \GL_n(\mathbb{A})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+program"} Langlands program
            in geometric terms (similar to the ones used in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
            over a function field) using the classifying stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BU(n)
            of principal
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
